{"ok": true, "messages": [{"ts": "1759189388.874759", "type": "message", "text": "just install the latest version. Unity hub will automatically open the project using the correct one when it is time.", "channel": "C0880U9751A", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759189361.525409", "type": "message", "text": "we haven't merged it yet. I'll let you know", "channel": "C0880U9751A", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1759175129.233219", "type": "message", "text": "<!here> can all Unity users please download this Unity version. We will be upgrading the project shortly.", "channel": "C0880U9751A", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758908698.346369", "type": "message", "text": "Seems like a half day task to add 'HP scale' or 'HP override' to level design tool.", "channel": "C0880U9751A", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758905638.539139", "type": "message", "text": "Ok great. This sounds like a great idea then. Can do remote at later time for the bonus.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758905611.787189", "type": "message", "text": "oh ok", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758905605.723179", "type": "message", "text": "like not uploaded to S3?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758905599.172519", "type": "message", "text": "ohh you guys mean using local Addressables", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758905563.306769", "type": "message", "text": "I think our build size might drop by like 80mb", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758905363.341129", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0032_SLACK_ID> The iOS memory seems like a guess. Will LiveOps to addressables do the trick you think? Do we have to go after the objects and monsters?

I should note that we currently don't have addressables in ZM. We will need to set up the addressable manager stuff from DD. So There is some more lifting than just making things into an addressable.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758848169.753889", "type": "message", "text": "The code looks like it plays both at the same time. Ok. If [USERNAME_37176] says it's good then it's good.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758838449.812699", "type": "message", "text": "We can leave it for now but just think about how we might fix it.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758838413.466729", "type": "message", "text": "If we were to start multiple tutorials it would be def be a problem.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758838333.037069", "type": "message", "text": "Ok.  The AI made a comment about the tutorial queuing multiple at once.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835593.463079", "type": "message", "text": "I think something like this might be cleaner:
```private void PlayLevelCompleteVFX()
{
    if (LevelManager.Instance.HasCompletedPreviousLevel())
    {
        // Check if VFX has already been shown for this level
        int currentLevel = PlayerPrefs.GetInt("Level", 0);
        string vfxKey = $"LevelCompleteVFX_Shown_{currentLevel}";

        if (!PlayerPrefs.GetInt(vfxKey, 0).Equals(1))
        {
            BlockInput();
            Debug.Log("[RewardVFXManager] Detected level completed. Playing coin VFX...");

            var req = new RewardVFXRequest
            {
                Type = ERewardType.Coins,
                Amount = CoinsManager.CoinsPerWin,
                Anchor = transform,
                WorldPosition = transform.position,
                WorldRotation = Quaternion.identity,
                HasWorldPose = true
            };

            PlayBatch(new List&lt;RewardVFXRequest&gt; { req });

            // Mark VFX as shown for this level
            PlayerPrefs.SetInt(vfxKey, 1);
            PlayerPrefs.Save();
        }
    }
}```", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835569.151229", "type": "message", "text": "Back to the PR review. It seems very weird that a [USERNAME_37174] would be resetting what the LastLevelCompleted is.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835511.171779", "type": "message", "text": "I was copying and pasting from chatgpt before but this is 10x better.", "channel": "D051LNQSFGQ", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758835497.424999", "type": "message", "text": "for example you put it in ‘agent’ mode and just say:

