{"ok": true, "messages": [{"ts": "1759249488.495439", "type": "message", "text": "i think we should squeeze in the fix for that issue if it's an easy fix. annoying and players can see that for 10 times in a day if they make it that far.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1759249488.495439"}, {"ts": "1758905363.341129", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0032_SLACK_ID> The iOS memory seems like a guess. Will LiveOps to addressables do the trick you think? Do we have to go after the objects and monsters?

I should note that we currently don't have addressables in ZM. We will need to set up the addressable manager stuff from DD. So There is some more lifting than just making things into an addressable.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758905363.341129"}, {"ts": "1758903616.346579", "type": "message", "text": "After I skipped the zombie lane tutorial, ı got the exception and skipping couldn’t claim the ice cream. <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID>   ", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758903616.346579"}, {"ts": "1758827960.705049", "type": "message", "text": "and both colliders are equal", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827946.430599", "type": "message", "text": "I was able to see this one in my first play", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827933.392849", "type": "message", "text": "which may cause performance issues as the colliders are quite complex", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827921.413599", "type": "message", "text": "looks like we can have objects that have more than 1 click collider", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758827895.596809", "type": "message", "text": "", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823160.030389", "type": "message", "text": "It could very well be an OS bug that we can't fix.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823142.221059", "type": "message", "text": "I think on Samsung devices, when you trigger that prompt, or about to, it disables the audio, because the permission dialog is an OS window, and it's an equivalent of homing out. So the app thinks it's in the background, at least from an audio standpoint", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758823108.379949", "type": "message", "text": "OK Fortress Merge also has the weird sound bug. So I was playing, and suddenly my audio disappears... I don't know why, nothing happened on screen. Then I force quit and restart my app, the moment I restart, I get the Push notification permission prompt.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758767858.307829", "type": "message", "text": "Yeah go for it. Once it’s merged we can trigger a testflight build and then can submit to Apple. It will take a few days to go live ", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765800.031519", "type": "message", "text": "do you think we can update the build version that the players are testing so we can gather new data?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765779.197199", "type": "message", "text": "and also added a skip tutorial button that appears after 10 seconds in the same tutorial step", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765741.130789", "type": "message", "text": "meaning the tutorial isnt showing anymore and the player is free to play", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758765726.644559", "type": "message", "text": "Not in the logs... I added a new analytics event that is invoked when the tutorial object is destroyed", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758763902.253029", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Any updates on the bugs? See anything strange?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758751463.920129", "type": "message", "text": "it’s a known thing that some event packs get dropped for some users occasioanlly, it happens to every game every user. It’s supposed to be a small percent but it happens - just a reminder on this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0038_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758751463.920129"}, {"ts": "1758746963.720009", "type": "message", "text": "And it's evident There was a restart because of the login and splash screen after level 2, but the left_level 2 event never fired off, so it would suggest that it's a pretty severe crash that the app can't even send off anything", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758746963.720009"}, {"ts": "1758746923.853549", "type": "message", "text": "This tells me There was a gap in their log, like Leonard's friend", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758746915.653289", "type": "message", "text": "I think something at the start of a level is crashing people, this user, started level 3, didn't finish level 3, but they have a begin level 2 event, but no left level 2 event, despite being able to start level 3:", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744890.526289", "type": "message", "text": "Invisible button", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744887.062759", "type": "message", "text": "Time based, I dont know", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758744881.531029", "type": "message", "text": "And something that allows them to skip tutorial", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741900.550579", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> can you add track item match too?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758741305.545019", "subtype": "thread_broadcast"}, {"ts": "1758741639.564949", "type": "message", "text": "just to discard the possibility", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741621.195989", "type": "message", "text": "we could even disable tutorials completely", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741498.293709", "type": "message", "text": "Maybe even 50% of the users are hit by this", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741473.290079", "type": "message", "text": "But the gist is that I would say 25% of the players are hit by this issue between level 3, 4, and 5. Once you make it through you're probably gonna be OK. So it's like a filter for buggy users", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741426.226829", "type": "message", "text": "Im adding more events to track correctness of each step that can act as blocker", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741424.791859", "type": "message", "text": "It could be some sort of initialization of something", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741413.330639", "type": "message", "text": "I dont even think it is the FTUE anymore, I might be wrong though", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741413.079659", "type": "message", "text": "But if it says "stop game" or "enemy start", I am unclear as to what happened next", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741399.304189", "type": "message", "text": "I would assume if they quit at "Waiting for highlight to fade", it's likely they didn't get to match a single item", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741334.346719", "type": "message", "text": "Because all these "crashes" it's a bit unclear the FTUE happened, did they just get stuck? Or were they at least able to match some items before restarting", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758741305.545019", "type": "message", "text": "<@EMPLOYEE_0025_SLACK_ID> <@EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID> Is There a good way to just record actual item click on or a set of item was removed from the board as an event? And we just plug it into level 1-5", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID", "thread_ts": "1758741305.545019"}, {"ts": "1758738754.255909", "type": "message", "text": "Leonard also had a friend, that had his game froze for good, and had to restart his app. This was during his first attempt at endless mode level. The log registered NOTHING. Meaning we didn't see him start/stop endless level, even though every user is forced to play it at least once.  Once Leonard's friend restarted, his log just continued to the next level, as if he skipped several steps, a giant gap in his log, like he got his drink spiked.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758738690.388049", "type": "message", "text": "So a lot of the problems we are seeing, is we see user engagement events happening mid level, or numerous times, repeatedly, at odd intervals. We were able to confirm that user_engagement event is working as it should. Our play test cloud video literally had a lady that took a face time call at level 7, and sure enough that backgrounding of the app created a user engagement event right on the dot.", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758738635.046079", "type": "message", "text": "Google truncates the user session with a "user_engagement" which records the duration of that session. The truncate happens when the app is put into the background for 1 second or more", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0016_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758737369.238919", "type": "message", "text": "user engagement means the game is stopped with various reasons, it can be a phone call, checking notifications, putting app to the background pr killing the app etc. then it sums up seconds between two user engagement event", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0012_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758737276.062599", "type": "message", "text": "do we know if the users with problems also stop in the user_engagement step?", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, {"ts": "1758737253.190019", "type": "message", "text": "well", "channel": "C08R27X0EAH", "user": "EMPLOYEE_0003_SLACK_ID"}, 